 ## Background
-Origin: Grendel-GS and TideGS are recent developments in 3D Gaussian Splatting optimization, as surveyed in [S1, unofficial].
-History: Part of the ongoing effort to scale 3DGS to larger scenes.
-Usage: Used in large-scale 3D reconstruction and dynamic scene modeling.
+Grendel-GS was introduced as part of the development of out-of-core and distributed optimization methods for 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the memory limitations of standard 3DGS training by distributing the Gaussian list across multiple GPUs.
